<title>JAPAN: Japan Dec industrial output rises 0.3 pct -- MITI.</title>
<headline>Japan Dec industrial output rises 0.3 pct -- MITI.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's industrial production in December rose a preliminary 0.3 percent from the previous month on a seasonally adjusted basis, the Ministry of International Trade and Industry (MITI) said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>MITI said in a statement that industrial output was on an upward trend.</p>
<p>Industrial production in the October-December period rose 3.3 percent from the previous quarter and rose 4.9 percent on a year-on-year basis.  </p>
<p>A breakdown of the preliminary monthly figures follows:</p>
<p>Seasonally adjusted month-on-month (in pct), index base 1990:</p>
<p>				  DEC	MONTH AGO     DEC INDEX</p>
<p> Output			 +0.3	-1.4	 100.4</p>
<p> Shipments		    +0.0	-0.5	 102.5</p>
<p> Inventories		  -0.4	-0.9	 107.0</p>
<p>Inventories to</p>
<p>    Shipments ratio	 -1.2	+1.4	 111.4</p>
<p>Unadjusted year-on-year (in pct):</p>
<p>				  DEC	MONTH AGO</p>
<p> Output			 +3.9	+4.5</p>
<p> Shipments		    +4.5	+5.4</p>
<p> Inventories		  -1.9	-0.7</p>
<p>Inventories to</p>
<p>    Shipments ratio	-4.6	-4.0</p>
<p>The following is a breakdown of MITI's forecasts for manufacturers' output:</p>
<p>Seasonally adjusted, month-on-month (in pct):</p>
<p>		     JAN forecast   FEB forecast</p>
<p>		     +5.4	     -2.9</p>
